# Notebooks: keep the .ipynb files but never commit kernel state output
# (uncomment if you want this; defaults to keeping outputs)
# *.ipynb

# --- CUDA / Profiling artifacts -----------------------------------------
# Profile outputs (*.nsys-rep, *.ncu-rep, *.qdrep*, *.qdstrm, *.sqlite) are
# tracked via Git LFS — see .gitattributes. They are real experiment data,
# not throw-away build output, so we DO commit them.
core.*

# Hand-built CUDA extension caches (load_inline / setuptools)
torch_extensions/
.cache/

# --- Per-experiment results that shouldn't be committed ------------------
# By default we DO commit small svgs / csvs under playground/**/results/
# because they're cited from blog posts. Uncomment the next line to flip
# that policy:
# playground/**/results/
